diff --git a/share/man/man4/bridge.4 b/share/man/man4/bridge.4
index 7e44c3773..f0ee4c894 100644
--- a/share/man/man4/bridge.4
+++ b/share/man/man4/bridge.4
@@ -455,6 +455,48 @@ interface and not to the bridge members.
 Enabling
 .Va net.link.bridge.pfil_local_phys
 will let you do the additional filtering on the physical interface.
+.Sh IGMP SNOOPING
+The
+.Nm
+driver can observe IPv4 IGMP membership reports to learn which member
+ports have listeners for a given multicast group and prune multicast
+forwarding to only those ports.
+This is disabled by default; forwarding falls back to flooding whenever no
+listener state is known, for non-IP multicast, and for exempt link-local
+control traffic.
+The following
+.Xr sysctl 8
+variables control and observe this behavior:
+.Bl -tag -width indent
+.It Va net.link.bridge.igmp_snooping
+Set to
+.Li 1
+to enable IGMP snooping so that IPv4 multicast with known listener state is
+pruned to the interested member ports.
+Set to
+.Li 0
+(the default) to disable learning and forwarding-path pruning; all multicast
+is flooded as it was before snooping existed.
+This variable is per-VNET and may be set as a tunable.
+.It Va net.link.bridge.mdb_entries
+Read-only count of multicast group entries currently held in the multicast
+database (MDB).
+.It Va net.link.bridge.mdb_prune_hits
+Read-only count of IPv4 multicast frames that were forwarded to a pruned set
+of MDB listeners rather than flooded.
+.It Va net.link.bridge.mdb_flood_fallback
+Read-only count of IPv4 multicast frames that were flooded because no MDB
+listener state existed for the group.
+.It Va net.link.bridge.mdb_parse_reject
+Read-only count of malformed or unsupported IGMP control packets rejected by
+the snooping parser.
+.It Va net.link.bridge.mdb_expired
+Read-only count of MDB listener entries removed because their membership aged
+out.
+.El
+.Pp
+Writing any value to one of the read-only counters resets it to zero.
+The counters are per-VNET.
 .Sh NETMAP
 .Xr netmap 4
 applications may open a bridge interface in emulated mode.
